---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import Prose from "../../components/Prose.astro";

const title = "Connect Fastmail Calendar to Pikos";
const description = "Sync a Fastmail calendar into Pikos over CalDAV. Make an app password, use caldav.fastmail.com, and your events arrive as pages you can take notes on. Read-only.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-8 py-20">

    <a href="/calendar-sync" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-neutral-400 transition-colors hover:text-primary-500 dark:text-neutral-500 dark:hover:text-primary-400">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"/></svg>
      Calendar sync
    </a>

    <article>
      <h1 class="mt-8 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50">Connect Fastmail Calendar</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-neutral-400 dark:text-neutral-500">Standard CalDAV. Two steps, and one of them is making a password.</p>

      <Prose class="mt-10">

        <p>
          Sync is read-only and opt-in. Your events come into Pikos as pages you can write on, and nothing you do in Pikos is ever sent back to Fastmail. Connecting it cannot change your calendar.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Make an app password</h2>

        <p>
          In Fastmail, go to <strong>Settings</strong>, then <strong>Privacy &amp; Security</strong>, then <strong>App Passwords</strong>, and create a new one. Give it access to calendars (CalDAV) and name it "Pikos".
        </p>

        <p>
          Your normal Fastmail password won't work here. Fastmail requires an app password for CalDAV, which is the safer arrangement anyway: you can delete it later to cut Pikos off without changing your login.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Connect in Pikos</h2>

        <p>
          Open Settings with <code>Cmd+,</code>, go to the <strong>Calendar Sync</strong> tab, click <strong>Add account</strong> and choose <strong>CalDAV</strong>. Fill in:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>Server URL</strong> &mdash; <code>https://caldav.fastmail.com</code></li>
          <li><strong>Username</strong> &mdash; your full Fastmail address</li>
          <li><strong>Password</strong> &mdash; the app password from step 1</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Pikos discovers your calendars from that base URL, so there's no per-calendar address to hunt down. Turn on the ones you want; each gets a folder and a colour. The password goes into the system keychain rather than a file Pikos owns.
        </p>

        <h2>What to expect afterwards</h2>

        <p>
          Pikos brings in the past week and everything ahead of it. Older events stay in Fastmail, so a freshly connected account looks thinner than the calendar you're used to.
        </p>

        <p>
          Title, time and recurrence are locked to the source. The notes you add are yours and sync never overwrites them. Turning a calendar off removes the mirrored events and keeps anything you wrote.
        </p>

        <h2>Other CalDAV providers</h2>

        <p>
          The same form works with any standard CalDAV server, including Nextcloud, Radicale, mailbox.org and Posteo. Find your provider's base CalDAV URL in their help pages, usually something like <code>https://caldav.yourprovider.com</code>, and use an app password if they offer one.
        </p>

      </Prose>

      <div class="mt-16 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 px-6 py-6 dark:border-neutral-800 dark:bg-neutral-900">
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">
          How synced events behave in full, plus iCloud and Google, is on the <a href="/calendar-sync" class="font-medium text-primary-500 hover:underline dark:text-primary-400">calendar sync page</a>. Don't have Pikos yet? It's a <a href="/download" class="font-medium text-primary-500 hover:underline dark:text-primary-400">free download</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

    </article>

  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>
